  "body": "Sets the v0.4.26 freeze anchors in `integration-candidate.json` so the connector consumer graph is consistent with the ecosystem core pins.\n\n**Change (o115b finding, `evidence/board-2026-10-24/o115b-freeze.md`)**\n- demo: `896dc3c` (stale) -> `25c319697fd3d89d894943e0f44cd3d5dde8b198`\n- console: `PENDING-FREEZE-DEMO...` -> `69d1d14007fa43dc0c0457c3347280be7f802818`\n- core: `2adae47a` left untouched (repo contract pins it; no update required)\n\n**Why**\n- `release-integration.yml:31` asserts `re.fullmatch('[0-9a-f]{40}', candidate['console'])`. main's `PENDING-FREEZE-DEMO` value fails this; the frozen Console SHA passes.\n- Keeps the connector candidate aligned with the core `consumer-pins.json` (#1050) ecosystem graph so pre-release.yml:117/:122 sees a consistent four-repo DAG.\n\n**Scope**\n- One file, two keys only. No runtime matrix, no product code. `go vet ./...`, `go build ./...`, `go test ./internal/...` all green locally.\n\n**Not done**\n- No merge (merge is a Codex maintainer lane, per owner rule). Open for review/approval.\n",
